=20

Dear Nadia

=20

I am sorry you remain so unwell.=20

=20

The current position is that my firm is owed around =C2=A312,000. I remind you =
that under the terms of the letter of instruction dated 24 January 2024 (att=
ached), you agreed to liquidate your 401K and pay USD30,000 to my firm=E2=80=99s c=
lient account and provide a bank guarantee. You did not comply with those te=
rms. If you had complied with the terms, I would have sufficient money both =
to discharge the outstanding fees and continue to act until the liquid sums =
had been used.

=20

If we are reinstructed, then the fees will depend on what we are instructed=
 to do. If it is simply to appear in court for the judgment then Brent will =
charge a refresher which I anticipate will be =C2=A38,000. My fees will be incur=
red on an hourly basis. Brent will then proceed to draft the court=E2=80=99s order=
 but that will be a simple process of translating the judgment of the court =
into the court=E2=80=99s order.  It will not be a case of trying to renegotiate or=
 relitigate what the Judge has decided.=20

=20

If I am reinstructed, and you ask me to instruct Brent then he will not cha=
rge you for carriage of the order (i.e. drafting it in liaison with the othe=
r side). That would be included within the brief fee. Obviously, if he has t=
o go to court then he will charge for that (alongside any other consultation=
s that you require). The difficulty for him, I envisage, is that because he =
does not act on a direct access basis, he would need to be instructed by me =
which would require you to instruct me. He could not just otherwise draft th=
e order because he would be without instructions from you. I say this becaus=
e I want to make clear that neither he nor I are attempting to charge you fo=
r something (i.e. the drafting of the order) which would otherwise have form=
ed part of the brief fee on the basis of the original instruction. I hope th=
is is clear.

=20

To reiterate, the fees which would be incurred to attend a hearing where ju=
dgment is handed down to be in the region of =C2=A35,000 for me and =C2=A38,000 for =
Brent. There will also be my fees incurred on an hourly rate for any work I =
do with Brent and you on the order. This may be 6 hours work at around =C2=A33k.=
 The total cost will be =C2=A316,000 on the basis that there is a hearing for th=
e judgment. Less if there is not but at present we do not know how judgment =
will be handed down.

=20

If the judgment is handed down in writing, and there is no hearing then any=
 time will be incurred which does not relate to the simple drafting of the c=
ourt=E2=80=99s order will be charged on an hourly basis by Brent and I.=20

=20

In any event, in order to resume my firm=E2=80=99s instruction the outstanding fe=
es (c.=C2=A312k) will need to be discharged and I will require a payment on acco=
unt of =C2=A316,000.

=20

If you have any questions, please let me know.


Very best

